{"eerie":{"id":"d32abe1a-c6d5-4263-8966-d83449fd6168","word":"eerie","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"inspiring fear, especially in a mysterious or shadowy way","word":"estranho"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"inspiring fear, especially in a mysterious or shadowy way","word":"assustador"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"inspiring fear, especially in a mysterious or shadowy way","word":"esquisito"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"The eerie sounds seemed to come from the graveyard after midnight.","bold_text_offsets":[[4,9]],"type":"example","id":"9a0f39ed-67e8-47fe-9176-714224e05624"},{"text":"An eerie feeling came over me.","ref":"1899 February, Joseph Conrad, “The Heart of Darkness”, in Blackwood’s Edinburgh Magazine, volume CLXV, number M, New York, N.Y.: The Leonard Scott Publishing Company, […], →OCLC, part I, page 200:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[3,8]],"id":"1fe16c3e-e146-4f07-9115-798bd94aab4b"},{"text":"Dan was beginning to feel very depressed when suddenly the eerie howl of a dingo rang out[.]","ref":"1943, H. Lorna Bingham, The Lost Tribe, Sydney: Winn and Co., page 13, column 2:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[59,64]],"id":"9dd295a3-ac34-4d01-a7a5-2b408391c002"},{"text":"I was working in the lab late one night / When my eyes beheld an eerie sight / For my monster, from his slab, began to rise / And suddenly, to my surprise / He did the Mash / He did the Monster Mash.","ref":"1962, “Monster Mash”, Bobby \"Boris\" Pickett and Lenny Capizzi (lyrics), performed by Bobby (Boris) Pickett and The Crypt-Kickers:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[65,70]],"id":"e42f74a8-3ae8-45d2-9069-ba85a0475e73"},{"text":"The whole city is immersed in a dystopian-looking smog: urban streets in sepia, emptier than usual, bathed in an eerie quiet.","ref":"2023 June 7, Samira Asma-Sadeque, “‘It’s too much’: New Yorkers don masks or stay 